  question: 'How Should Payments, Deposits and Financing Be Handled?',
  answer: [
    'Payment should follow clarity, not pressure. Before a deposit, you should understand the written scope, standard features, selected upgrades, exclusions, site assumptions, deposit purpose, payment timing, change-order process and final-payment expectations.',
    'Payment milestones should match the project’s size and complexity. Financing can help you understand monthly cost and total obligation, but it never replaces a written construction scope.',
    'The safe order: define what is being built, define what is not included, confirm site assumptions, document upgrades, explain how changes are handled, then document deposit and payment timing.',
  ],
  sections: [
    {
      type: 'steps', id: 'sequence', eyebrow: 'The Right Budget Sequence', title: 'Scope Comes Before Money Changes Hands', nav: 'Budget Sequence',
